.nvimlog
# Neovim drops this in whatever directory it was started from, so it lands in
# the source tree whenever nvim is opened here. It is a transient warning log,
# and without an ignore rule chezmoi also treats it as a file to deploy.
nvim.log

# Work-only agent config. The `origin` remote is a PUBLIC GitHub repo, and
# .chezmoiignore only gates DEPLOYMENT — everything in the source tree still
# gets committed and published by dotfiles-publish. So anything naming internal
# orgs, repos, or services has to be excluded from git here, not there.
#
# Consequence: these files are machine-local and NOT BACKED UP. See CLAUDE.md
# "Agent config" for what belongs in them.
dot_claude/rules/carepilot.md
# Reserved: a self-contained work-only Codex profile, used as `codex -p work`.
# Codex profiles do NOT compose (`-p` layers exactly one file over the base), so
# a work profile would have to duplicate main.config.toml. Prefer putting
# work-only Codex settings in the untracked ~/.codex/config.toml instead.
dot_codex/work.config.toml

# Secret-bearing files that must never be committed again. Both of these WERE
# committed once, in September 2025, and their contents remain readable in the
# public history of `origin`, because deleting a file later does not remove the
# blob. The gitleaks gate in dotfiles-publish scans only `origin/main..HEAD` by
# design, so it structurally cannot re-flag history that was already pushed.
# These two entries are the tripwire that stops a repeat.
#
# Nothing references either path any more. Secrets now come from 1Password via
# onepasswordRead in the templates, which keeps them out of the source tree
# entirely rather than relying on an ignore rule.
dot_zsh_secrets
dot_config/raycast/private_config.json
